Emne: RE: Nodelaeser

Hi Bo,

Here is an update regarding the Nodelaeser braille conversion. Geert Maesse=
n, a professional braille music transcriber at Dedicon, Netherlands has bee=
n so kind to do a good and quite thorough research on the braille conversio=
n of version 4 of Nodeleaser.

I send you the results, it may be of use for your developement team. Unfort=
unately it is in Dutch but I hope standard translation will be appropriate.=
 (Full results including testfiles can be provided).

Raw conclusion: the braille conversion is very promising, basically it is O=
K but work needs to be done to make the output (easier) readable, following=
 standard braille rules.
This counts especially for multipart pieces.
However, musicians that use single part sheet music and not too complex pie=
ces (e.g. amateur flute players, or choir singers), can already use and ben=
efit from the conversion as it is now.

Good to mention that Geert is willing to help / think / test with future de=
velopments.
I have included his mailadress in cc. Feel free to contact him.

It would be great if Nodelaeser keeps on developing. And it would be great =
if we could stay in touch.

Kind regards,
Marc Stovers
Roya Dutch Visio

Van: Marc Stovers
