Onderwerp: RE: Nodelaeser

Hi Bo,

Thanks for your reply. We have tried out Nodelaeser and our first implressi=
on is very positive. We are very enthousiastic about this product and we th=
ink it can be very useful for visual impaired people, the blind in particul=
ar.

One thing we unfortunately cannot check ourselves due to the lack of specif=
ic expertise is the quality of the braille conversion. However, sounds like=
 a very unique feature, as we do know this is a complex job to do and sever=
al attempts have been made worldwide the past decade (and failed).
So were really interested in this feature and we'd like to ask you if you h=
ave specific test or user feedback about the Music XML to Braille conversio=
n? This would save us all the work of testing ourselves (and funding it).
Would be grateful if you could provide this information.

Furthermore, contact info of the Dutch co-operators would be appreciated.

And a question: we tried out version 4, you mentioned verson 5. Is it corre=
ct that version 5 is not available yet? (download file says 4.0.0.0).

I'm considering to publish a short review on the Dutch platform kennisporta=
al.visio.org<https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=3Dhttps%3A=
%2F%2Fkennisportaal.visio.org%2F&data=3D05%7C01%7C%7Ca8753836961d4dfdc53208=
da34accc29%7C769058ab4487418f8b6cf4b48243edd7%7C0%7C0%7C637880214167843539%=
7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWw=
iLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&sdata=3DFrhFwSbZSamn4zZd42IR1ACrvjtDKHqS0Ou=
0PsRD%2FO8%3D&reserved=3D0> , the practical knowledge base and self service=
 portal for the visual impaired in the Netherlands, from which I am the edi=
tor and content manager. So also in this respect any test & experience info=
rmation would be useful.
The article would also be published in Infovisie MagaZIEN, a Belgium magazi=
ne on tech for visually impaired.

Thank you very much, in advance,

Marc Stovers
